{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39288","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:44.840309+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Thanks for the great report! This is a great way to use Claude / other tools.\n\nThe first bug is easy but the scan bug less so. The issue is that we use a helper function to batch the body jaxpr, and to facilitate fixpoints on the carry that helper only supports batched-on-leading and not-batched. Values batched on non-leading just get transposed. But we can’t do that for refs!","created_at":"2026-07-18T20:09:11Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/39288#issuecomment-5012746181","id":5012746181,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39288","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc8AAAABKshvxQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/5012746181/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-07-18T20:09:11Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/5012746181","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1458824?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattjj","id":1458824,"login":"mattjj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTg4MjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1458824?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattjj","id":1458824,"login":"mattjj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTg4MjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1458824?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattjj","id":1458824,"login":"mattjj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTg4MjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Description\n\nPassing a `Ref` as a `vmap`-batched argument works with `in_axes=0`, including reading and writing it from inside a `lax.scan` that closes over it (this case was fixed in 0.10.1 by #37113). With `in_axes=1`, however, several basic operations fail on 0.11.0, apparently in the handling of the `TransformedRef` view created by the non-leading batch axis.\n\n## Failures\n\n### Full-ref write of a batched value\n\nNote the error message: expected and actual shapes are transposes of each other.\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\ndef f(r, x):\n    r[...] = x\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((2, 3)))\njax.vmap(f, in_axes=(1, 0))(ref, jnp.ones((3, 2)))\n```\n\n```text\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip3.py\", line 8, in <module>\n    jax.vmap(f, in_axes=(1, 0))(ref, jnp.ones((3, 2)))\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip3.py\", line 5, in f\n    r[...] = x\n    ~^^^^^\n  File \"/Users/giacomo/.cache/uv/archive-v0/loSAW86OszREXv0G/lib/python3.14/site-packages/jax/_src/numpy/array_methods.py\", line 1532, in op\n    return getattr(self.aval, f\"_{name}\")(self, *args)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: Invalid shape for `swap`. Ref shape: (2, 3). Expected shape: (2, 3). Value shape: (3, 2). Transforms: (). \n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n```\n\n### Scan closing over the ref\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\ndef f(r):\n    def body(carry, x):\n        r[0] += 1\n        return None, None\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((2, 3)))\njax.vmap(f, in_axes=1)(ref)\n```\n\n```text\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip4.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    jax.vmap(f, in_axes=1)(ref)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip4.py\", line 9, in f\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n    ~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'Ref' object has no attribute 'transpose'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n```\n\n### Scan closing over the ref, under `jit`\n\nSame as above under `jit`, different error:\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\ndef f(r):\n    def body(carry, x):\n        r[0] += 1\n        return None, None\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((2, 3)))\njax.jit(jax.vmap(f, in_axes=1))(ref)\n```\n\n```text\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip5.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    jax.jit(jax.vmap(f, in_axes=1))(ref)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip5.py\", line 9, in f\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n    ~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: Triggering __jax_array__() during abstractification is no longer supported. To avoid this error, either explicitly convert your object using jax.numpy.array(), or register your object as a pytree.\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n```\n\nOn jax 0.10.1 this last case raises a different error:\n\n```text\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip5.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    jax.jit(jax.vmap(f, in_axes=1))(ref)\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/issue_snips/snip5.py\", line 9, in f\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n    ~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\njax._src.state.types.TransformedRefAvalError: TransformedRefs cannot be abstractified.\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n```\n\n## Controls\n\nEach control is a failure above with a single change: the batch axis moved to 0, or the scan removed.\n\n### Full-ref write of a batched value, batch axis 0\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\ndef f(r, x):\n    r[...] = x\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((3, 2)))\njax.vmap(f, in_axes=(0, 0))(ref, jnp.ones((3, 2)))\nprint(ref[...])\n```\n\n```text\n[[1. 1.]\n [1. 1.]\n [1. 1.]]\n```\n\n### Scan closing over the ref, batch axis 0\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\ndef f(r):\n    def body(carry, x):\n        r[0] += 1\n        return None, None\n    lax.scan(body, None, length=1)\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((2, 3)))\njax.vmap(f, in_axes=0)(ref)\nprint(ref[...])\n```\n\n```text\n[[1. 0. 0.]\n [1. 0. 0.]]\n```\n\n### The scan body write alone, batch axis 1\n\nThe indexed write from the scan failures works at batch axis 1 when it's not inside a loop:\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\ndef f(r):\n    r[0] += 1\n\nref = jax.new_ref(jnp.zeros((2, 3)))\njax.vmap(f, in_axes=1)(ref)\nprint(ref[...])\n```\n\n```text\n[[1. 1. 1.]\n [0. 0. 0.]]\n```\n\n## Note\n\nWritten by Claude Fable 5, edited & checked by a human.\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:    0.11.0\njaxlib: 0.11.0\nnumpy:  2.5.1\npython: 3.14.0 (main, Oct 14 2025, 21:10:22) [Clang 20.1.4 ]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Darwin', release='25.5.0', version='Darwin Kernel Version 25.5.0: Tue Jun  9 22:18:58 PDT 2026; root:xnu-12377.121.10~1/RELEASE_ARM64_T6000', machine='arm64')\n```\n","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39288/comments","created_at":"2026-07-18T08:26:09Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39288/events","html_url":"https://github.com/j